From 5664ca74bdd3f17761c21d713bd9c3784e4b7eb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gus bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:19:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 109/145] media: meson: vdec: return input credit on unmatched
 timestamp offsets

amvdec_dst_buf_done_offset() delivers a decoded frame even when no
timestamp record matches its offset, but returns esparser input credit
only when a record was found. Each unmatched completion therefore
leaves an extra unit in esparser_queued_bufs. Return the credit for
every delivered frame, as in the normal timestamp completion path.
Keep the existing mismatch diagnostic.

Prove the leak with an experimental module that skips the timestamp
lookup every fourth completion and independently toggles this
decrement. On the VIM3 HEVC path, the unfixed binary stops at 52
frames (49 in a repeat), with 13 injected misses and credit stuck at
16 for sixteen seconds. Changing only the fix parameter completes 240
frames within one second in both runs, despite 61 injected misses,
with credit ending at 3.

This does not explain the separately reported H.264 backward-seek/UI
stall. The counter throttle is gated to VP9/HEVC in this tree, and to
VP9 in local pristine v7.2. H.264 completes 240 frames with the
injected misses both with and without this fix. The reporter also
reports no unmatched-offset errors. Do not present this accounting
correction as a fix for that untraced stall.

Signed-off-by: gus bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
index b390e464f8ed..952d10915d27 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
@@ -505,8 +505,8 @@ void amvdec_dst_buf_done_offset(struct amvdec_session *sess,
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&sess->ts_spinlock, flags);
 
 	dst_buf_done(sess, vbuf, field, timestamp, timecode, vbuf_flags);
-	if (match)
-		atomic_dec(&sess->esparser_queued_bufs);
+	/* A completed frame releases input credit even without a timestamp. */
+	atomic_dec(&sess->esparser_queued_bufs);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(amvdec_dst_buf_done_offset);
 
-- 
